"JH" <no@email.com> writes:
> I seem to remember that in 341, if I pulled a lodestone out of a chest, then
> it didn't autocurse itself.  I just did that in 342, and it did autocurse
> itself.

Autocursing happens when the loadstone (note spelling) _leaves_ your
main inventory, not when it enters it. So, you're really asking about
the cursed status _on generation_ of a loadstone created in a chest :-)

It is possible (and this hasn't changed) for a loadstone created in a
container to be either cursed or uncursed. What's actually happened in
the latter case is that the game chose to generate rocks, which aren't
valid things to be created in containers, and so rerolled the type among
* items which _are_ valid, and happened to get a loadstone; the cursed
status isn't adjusted in this case, so the usual "loadstones are always
generated cursed" code isn't applied.

>  So originally,  I thought that the lack of autocursing was a
